  "description": "Δ_λ option D: LP-dual shadow-price selection for the H_{3A} Wedderburn refinement of ρ_K (deuteron, n=6, 11 partitions). Reformulates the underdetermined mass equation as an operator-selection LP per prop:operator-selection-lp; the dual variables y0_star / y_star are the *derived* per-irrep binding-energy shadow prices, replacing the arbitrary single-support / smallest-|Δ| heuristic of the Occam baseline. Cost vector is plancherel (Plancherel = 1/dim_q(λ); Frobenius = |χ^λ(β_D)|). Both costs reported. Sibling of PR #600 derivation race (A=Occam, B=co-Casimir, C=Demazure, D=this LP-dual, E=crystal).",
